{
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "lane-person",
      "type": "group",
      "label": "The person",
      "x": -1940,
      "y": -100,
      "width": 720,
      "height": 2000,
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "lane-project",
      "type": "group",
      "label": "A project agent  \u00b7  tier: consult",
      "x": -1180,
      "y": -100,
      "width": 720,
      "height": 1960,
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "lane-library",
      "type": "group",
      "label": "The library agent  \u00b7  tier: contribute",
      "x": -420,
      "y": -100,
      "width": 720,
      "height": 2060,
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "lane-scout",
      "type": "group",
      "label": "The unattended local-model scout",
      "x": 340,
      "y": -100,
      "width": 720,
      "height": 2060,
      "color": "3"
    },
    {
      "id": "lane-vault",
      "type": "group",
      "label": "The airlock, and the truth  \u00b7  tier: curate",
      "x": 1100,
      "y": -100,
      "width": 720,
      "height": 1980,
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "p0",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# The person\n\nYou own the sentence a reader acts on. **Nothing else in this system can write one.**",
      "x": -1900,
      "y": 0,
      "width": 640,
      "height": 160,
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "p1",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## 1 \u00b7 Find something\n\n```\nlibrarian web\nlibrarian query donor \"...\"\n```\n\nA catalogue, not a search box: drop-downs are built from the result set, and a count is the size of what survives choosing it.\n\nCounts reconcile. A constraint that removed the best answer says so, in red, at the top.",
      "x": -1900,
      "y": 200,
      "width": 640,
      "height": 300,
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## 2 \u00b7 Log what you used\n\n```\nlibrarian queue add <url> --why \"...\"\n```\n\nA URL is fine. Three answers: **already catalogued** (with the note), **queued**, **seen again**.\n\nLog it even if you rejected it \u2014 say so in `--why`. The queue is cheap; rediscovering the same dead end next quarter is not.",
      "x": -1900,
      "y": 540,
      "width": 640,
      "height": 300,
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "p3",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## 3 \u00b7 Review the airlock\n\n```\nlibrarian staging list\nlibrarian staging show <id>\n```\n\n`show` renders the note **exactly as it would be written**, so nothing is a surprise after the fact.",
      "x": -1900,
      "y": 880,
      "width": 640,
      "height": 240,
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "p4",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## 4 \u00b7 Promote\n\n```\nlibrarian staging promote <id> \\\n  --bottom-line \"...\" \\\n  --what-it-solves \"...\"\n```\n\nThe only write a reader ever sees. It **refuses without the interpretation**, and it runs the vault's own integrity checks *before* writing \u2014 a note the vault would reject is reported, not written.",
      "x": -1900,
      "y": 1160,
      "width": 640,
      "height": 320,
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "p5",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## 5 \u00b7 Maintain\n\n```\nlibrarian integrity\nlibrarian views --check\nlibrarian relevance --scenarios 0\nlibrarian staging rederive --deep\n```\n\nRun `rederive` after **any** taxonomy change: it replays the new rules over everything already staged, with no model calls and no network.",
      "x": -1900,
      "y": 1520,
      "width": 640,
      "height": 300,
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "j0",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# A project agent\n\n```\nlibrarian serve --tier consult\n```\n\nRuns inside `Mark-XLVIII`, `quantule_mapper`, `knowledge_compiler_engine`, `network_management` \u2014 not inside the vault.",
      "x": -1140,
      "y": 0,
      "width": 640,
      "height": 200,
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "j1",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## Ask before building\n\n`find_donor(need, constraints)`\n\nIf nothing fits, the reply says **\"nothing here covers this\"** as plainly as it reports a match.\n\nThat is a real answer. Do not treat a weak match as an endorsement.",
      "x": -1140,
      "y": 240,
      "width": 640,
      "height": 260,
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "j2",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## Log every source you touch\n\n`log_use(url, project, why)`\n\nOne call, no ceremony, nothing owed afterwards. The `why` is stored as *reported by you* \u2014 never as a fact about the project \u2014 and it is the only part of the eventual note that will come from real use rather than a README.",
      "x": -1140,
      "y": 540,
      "width": 640,
      "height": 300,
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "j3",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## Ask for what is missing\n\n`open_brief(project, need, disqualifiers, constraints)`\n\n**`disqualifiers` is required.** Not the topic \u2014 what a candidate must not assume, require or depend on.\n\n> RuView was found, researched and charted accurately, and still cost a leg of the project: its sense model assumes ESP32 input shape and the hardware is an Intel 5300. No taxonomy anticipates that. Only the asker knows it.",
      "x": -1140,
      "y": 880,
      "width": 640,
      "height": 380,
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "j4",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## Record what actually worked\n\n`record_application(...)`\n\n`what_the_catalogue_should_learn` is what turns a diary entry into a requirement.\n\nAny source it names that the catalogue does not hold is **queued automatically** \u2014 you do not log it twice.",
      "x": -1140,
      "y": 1300,
      "width": 640,
      "height": 280,
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "j5",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## What it cannot do\n\nWrite a note. By design: a resource note carries a sentence a reader acts on, and that is written by whoever stands behind it.",
      "x": -1140,
      "y": 1620,
      "width": 640,
      "height": 160,
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "l0",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# The library agent\n\n```\nlibrarian serve --tier contribute\n```\n\nHolds no path into `01-Resources/`. The reachable damage is a directory of JSON.",
      "x": -380,
      "y": 0,
      "width": 640,
      "height": 180,
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "l1",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## Take work\n\n```\nlist_briefs()  \u2192  claim_brief(id, agent)\nlist_queue()\n```\n\nA brief is *find me something that does X*. The queue is the commoner case: *someone is already using this and we have never heard of it*.",
      "x": -380,
      "y": 220,
      "width": 640,
      "height": 260,
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "l2",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## Screen against the brief\n\nOne cheap model call, asked negatively: **what does this text contradict?**\n\n`keep` \u00b7 `reject` \u00b7 **`unclear`**\n\nAsked whether something is suitable, a small model agrees. Asked for a contradiction, it has to point at a sentence. `unclear` is a normal answer \u2014 most texts will not say.",
      "x": -380,
      "y": 520,
      "width": 640,
      "height": 320,
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "l3",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## Stage what survives\n\n`propose_resource(repo_key, url, axes, evidence, ...)`\n\nFour refusals, each by name:\n\n- `EVIDENCE_REQUIRED` \u2014 nothing was fetched\n- `NO_SCHEMA_DRIFT` \u2014 axis value outside its enumeration\n- `STAGING_BEFORE_VAULT` \u2014 already charted; here is the note\n- `INTERPRETATION_IS_NOT_MACHINE_WORK`",
      "x": -380,
      "y": 880,
      "width": 640,
      "height": 340,
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "l4",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## Dispose of everything seen\n\n`decide_candidate(brief, repo, \"rejected\", reason)`\n\nThe reason **is** the negative result. *\"Sense model assumes ESP32 CSI shape\"* is worth more to the next search than most positive entries \u2014 and it exists only because something insisted on it here.",
      "x": -380,
      "y": 1260,
      "width": 640,
      "height": 300,
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "l5",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## Close\n\n`close_brief(id, summary)`\n\nRefuses while any candidate is undecided. `DOCUMENT_BEFORE_DESTROY`, one level up from the workbench.\n\n`--discard` exists, and is not silent: each dropped candidate is recorded with a reason.",
      "x": -380,
      "y": 1600,
      "width": 640,
      "height": 280,
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "s0",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# The local-model scout\n\n```\nlibrarian populate queue --limit N\nlibrarian populate brief <id>\n```\n\nLM Studio, roughly 110s per source, free. It stages; it never writes a note.",
      "x": 380,
      "y": 0,
      "width": 640,
      "height": 200,
      "color": "3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s1",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## Read, don't ask\n\nA fact is **never** put to a model. `derive` reads it:\n\n| axis | from |\n|---|---|\n| `license_class` | SPDX, else the LICENSE file |\n| `ecosystem` | the language |\n| `maturity_stage` | archived flag + push date |\n| `security_compliance` | keywords |\n| `agent_surface` | the path ladder \u2014 **0.958** |\n\n> Asked for a licence with `GPL-3.0` in the text above the question, a 4B model answered `Unknown`.",
      "x": 380,
      "y": 240,
      "width": 640,
      "height": 420,
      "color": "3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## Ask only what must be judged\n\nOne enumeration per call, temperature 0, no history, no knowledge of the pipeline.\n\n`confident: false` \u2192 **dropped, not recorded.**\n\n> A bigger model was *more confident and more wrong*: `qwen3-8b` answered `ecosystem: Web_Frontend`, confidently, citing its own evidence line `main language: Rust`.",
      "x": 380,
      "y": 700,
      "width": 640,
      "height": 340,
      "color": "3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## Describe from evidence\n\nWhat Is Inside \u00b7 Architecture & Mechanics \u00b7 Integration & Use Cases\n\nEvery bullet is checked against the text the model was given. An invented name is dropped.\n\n> The first run wrote *\"Uses tree-sitter for parsing\"* for a project whose documentation never mentions tree-sitter.",
      "x": 380,
      "y": 1080,
      "width": 640,
      "height": 300,
      "color": "3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## Never the interpretation\n\n`Bottom Line` and `What It Solves` are **refused** from any machine.\n\nA small model fills enumerations well and writes plausible mush \u2014 and mush passes every structural check there is.",
      "x": 380,
      "y": 1420,
      "width": 640,
      "height": 220,
      "color": "3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s5",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## Resume\n\nA killed run strands nothing: a claim nobody is holding is retaken by the next run.\n\n```\nlibrarian queue release <id>\n```",
      "x": 380,
      "y": 1680,
      "width": 640,
      "height": 200,
      "color": "3"
    },
    {
      "id": "v0",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# The airlock\n\n`.Data/staging/`\n\nNothing here is in the vault. Nothing here is indexed. Nothing here reaches a reader.",
      "x": 1140,
      "y": 0,
      "width": 640,
      "height": 180,
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "v1",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## Why the split is here\n\nIt follows the line the vault already draws between its layers:\n\n| step | who | produces |\n|---|---|---|\n| `propose` | any agent, incl. a local model | **data** |\n| `promote` | a person, or an agent that used it | **information** |\n\nFilling ten closed enumerations from a survey is constrained choice. Writing the sentence a reader acts on is not.",
      "x": 1140,
      "y": 220,
      "width": 640,
      "height": 360,
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "v2",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## readiness\n\nEvery proposal comes back saying what promotion *would* refuse \u2014 at propose time, while the agent still has the connection open.\n\n```\n{\"ready\": false,\n \"blocked_on\": [\"missing 'github_stars'\", ...]}\n```\n\nA proposal that sits in staging looking finished and can never be promoted is worse than a refused one.",
      "x": 1140,
      "y": 620,
      "width": 640,
      "height": 320,
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "v3",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## One validator, not two\n\nPromotion calls the **same three integrity checks** `librarian integrity` runs, on a one-note list \u2014 not a second copy of the rules that would drift from the first.",
      "x": 1140,
      "y": 980,
      "width": 640,
      "height": 200,
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "v4",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# 01-Resources/\n\n**The truth.**\n\nReached by exactly one tool \u2014 `promote_proposal`, tier `curate` \u2014 and only with a sentence somebody stands behind.",
      "x": 1140,
      "y": 1220,
      "width": 640,
      "height": 200,
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "v5",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## The tiers\n\n```\nconsult     reads + application records\ncontribute  + briefs, queue, staging\n            (cannot alter a note)\ncurate      + promotion\n```\n\nThe old guarantee was *exactly one tool writes*. Its honest successor is **what each write can reach**: seven write, two create a note, one creates a note in `01-Resources/` \u2014 and it is not in the tier a research agent runs at.",
      "x": 1140,
      "y": 1460,
      "width": 640,
      "height": 340,
      "color": "1"
    }
  ],
